      "updated": 1795621586000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ANY side channel the consumer writes (DLQ, retry topic, metrics, outbox) has its own at-least-once behaviour unless it is inside a real\nKafka transaction with the offset commit. That could close the gap for Kafka writes only; Postgres stays separate.",
      "originalText": "ANY side channel the consumer writes (DLQ, retry topic, metrics, outbox) has its own at-least-once behaviour unless it is inside a real Kafka transaction with the offset commit. That could close the gap for Kafka writes only; Postgres stays separate.",
